   "id": "fcb0d910-159f-492c-bf05-9b760e68eead",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "In NumPy, arrays don’t store mixed data types like normal Python lists. Instead, they use a single common data type, called \"dtype\".\n",
    "\n",
    "🔹 Common data types in NumPy\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Integer numbers → int32, int64\n",
    "\n",
    "float →  float32, float64\n",
    "       \n",
    "Boolean values →  bool\n",
    "        \n",
    "Complex nums → complex64, complex128\n",
    "        \n",
    "Strings → S (byte-str) & U (unicode-str)\n",
    "\n",
    "Object → generic python - object (mixed type data)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "* we can \"DOWNCAST\" the data types according to the desires\n",
    "\n",
    "       "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "6b640ef8-7dc5-4912-8772-3b101ce5aa3f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "47d48960-6905-4f4f-8c37-ec7397ff055b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[3.+5.j] complex128\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Example of complex numbers\n",
    "\n",
    "arr = np.array([3 + 5j])\n",
    "print(arr, arr.dtype)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "9439d0e5-e920-466f-b02c-82ca95ae3281",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[1 2 {3, 4} 'Wow'] object\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# List can store HETEROGENEOUS VALUES whereas, NumPy cannot\n",
    "\n",
    "arr = np.array([1, 2, {3, 4}, \"Wow\"])\n",
    "print(arr, arr.dtype)\n"
   ]
  }
